<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>UX Lens — Usability Audit & Redesign</title>

<style>
:root {
  --ink: #18212f;
  --muted: #667085;
  --line: #e4e7ec;
  --paper: #f6f7fb;
  --purple: #6658e8;
  --purple2: #eeeaff;
  --red: #b42318;
  --redbg: #fee4e2;
  --amber: #92400e;
  --amberbg: #fef0c7;
  --green: #067647;
  --greenbg: #dcfae6;
  --white: #ffffff;
  --shadow: 0 12px 32px #18212f0d;
}

* {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--paper);
  color: var(--ink);
  font: 15px/1.55 Inter, system-ui, sans-serif;
}

button {
  font: inherit;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.wrap {
  max-width: 1180px;
  margin: auto;
  padding: 28px 22px 60px;
}

header {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 16px;
  margin-bottom: 42px;
}

.brand {
  font-weight: 850;
  font-size: 22px;
  letter-spacing: -.04em;
}

.brand span {
  color: var(--purple);
}

.tag {
  font-size: 12px;
  color: var(--muted);
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  padding: 7px 11px;
  border-radius: 999px;
}

.hero {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1.2fr .8fr;
  gap: 36px;
  align-items: center;
  margin-bottom: 38px;
}

.eyebrow {
  color: var(--purple);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-size: 12px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: .12em;
}

.hero h1 {
  font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 58px);
  line-height: 1.02;
  letter-spacing: -.055em;
  margin: 12px 0 18px;
}

.hero p {
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 17px;
  max-width: 660px;
}

.actions {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 10px;
  margin-top: 22px;
}

.btn {
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 11px 16px;
  font-weight: 750;
}

.primary {
  background: var(--purple);
  color: white;
}

.secondary {
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  color: var(--ink);
}

.hero-art {
  background: #17152d;
  border-radius: 28px;
  padding: 22px;
  color: white;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  transform: rotate(1deg);
}

.art-top {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  color: #c8c5ef;
  font-size: 12px;
}

.art-title {
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: 800;
  margin: 18px 0;
}

.mini-row {
  display: flex;
  gap: 10px;
}

.mini-card {
  background: #292644;
  border: 1px solid #45415f;
  border-radius: 14px;
  padding: 14px;
  flex: 1;
}

.mini-card b {
  display: block;
  font-size: 24px;
}

.mini-card small {
  color: #c8c5ef;
}

.progress {
  height: 8px;
  background: #48445f;
  border-radius: 10px;
  margin-top: 16px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.progress span {
  display: block;
  width: 68%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #a9a0ff;
  border-radius: 10px;
}

nav {
  display: flex;
  gap: 8px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin: 24px 0 18px;
}

.tab {
  padding: 10px 14px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 11px;
  background: white;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-weight: 700;
}

.tab.active {
  background: var(--purple2);
  color: var(--purple);
  border-color: #d7d1ff;
}

.section {
  display: none;
}

.section.active {
  display: block;
}

.section-head {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: end;
  gap: 20px;
  margin: 28px 0 18px;
}

.section-head h2 {
  font-size: 28px;
  letter-spacing: -.04em;
  margin: 0;
}

.section-head p {
  margin: 4px 0 0;
  color: var(--muted);
}

.note {
  border: 1px solid #fedf89;
  background: #fffaeb;
  color: #7a2e0e;
  border-radius: 13px;
  padding: 14px 16px;
  margin: 16px 0 20px;
  font-size: 13px;
}

.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 16px;
}

.card {
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
  padding: 18px;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
}

.card h3 {
  margin: 0 0 8px;
  font-size: 17px;
}

.card p {
  color: var(--muted);
  margin: 0;
}

.pill {
  display: inline-block;
  border-radius: 999px;
  padding: 4px 9px;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 850;
  letter-spacing: .03em;
}

.critical {
  background: var(--redbg);
  color: var(--red);
}

.medium {
  background: var(--amberbg);
  color: var(--amber);
}

.low {
  background: var(--greenbg);
  color: var(--green);
}

.small-label {
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 850;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: .09em;
  color: var(--muted);
  margin-bottom: 7px;
}

.audit-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  background: white;
  border-radius: 16px;
  overflow: hidden;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
}

.audit-table th,
.audit-table td {
  text-align: left;
  vertical-align: top;
  padding: 13px 14px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
}

.audit-table th {
  background: #f0effb;
  font-size: 12px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: .05em;
}

.audit-table td {
  font-size: 13px;
}

.audit-table tr:last-child td {
  border-bottom: 0;
}

.boards {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 18px;
}

.board {
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
  background: white;
  padding: 16px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.board h3 {
  margin: 0 0 5px;
}

.board p {
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 13px;
  margin: 0 0 14px;
}

.browser {
  border: 1px solid #d9dce5;
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: white;
}

.browserbar {
  background: #f4f5f8;
  padding: 9px 12px;
  font-size: 11px;
  color: #7c8494;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #e3e6ed;
}

.shopnav {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  padding: 14px;
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: 800;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
}

.shopnav .links {
  font-weight: 500;
  color: #697386;
  display: flex;
  gap: 10px;
}

.shopbody {
  padding: 14px;
}

.shophero {
  padding: 18px 13px;
  border-radius: 9px;
  background: #f4e9db;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

.shophero h4,
.goodhero h4 {
  font-size: 22px;
  line-height: 1.1;
  margin: 0 0 7px;
}

.shophero h4 {
  max-width: 240px;
}

.shophero p {
  font-size: 11px;
  color: #68615b;
  margin: 0 0 12px;
}

.product-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 8px;
}

.product {
  position: relative;
  border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 7px;
}

.product .photo {
  height: 64px;
  border-radius: 5px;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f3e7dd, #d9c4ae);
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  font-size: 26px;
}

.product:nth-child(2) .photo {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e6e8dd, #b9c4ac);
}

.product:nth-child(3) .photo {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e6e3ef, #c7bfdc);
}

.product b {
  font-size: 10px;
  display: block;
  margin-top: 6px;
}

.product small {
  font-size: 9px;
  color: #687080;
}

.bad-marker {
  position: absolute;
  top: 5px;
  right: 5px;
  background: #b42318;
  color: white;
  font-size: 9px;
  padding: 3px 5px;
  border-radius: 4px;
}

.old-cta {
  background: #e3e3e3;
  color: #777;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 3px;
  padding: 5px 7px;
  font-size: 9px;
  margin-top: 5px;
}

.good-cta {
  background: #6558e8;
  color: white;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 8px 10px;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
}

.good-nav {
  display: flex;
  gap: 10px;
  align-items: center;
}

.search {
  flex: 1;
  border: 1px solid #d7d9e2;
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 8px;
  font-size: 10px;
  color: #6b7280;
  font-weight: 500;
}

.goodhero {
  background: #f1edff;
  padding: 18px 13px;
  border-radius: 10px;
  margin: 12px 0;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 10px;
  align-items: center;
}

.goodhero h4 {
  max-width: 210px;
}

.goodhero p {
  font-size: 11px;
  color: #5d5a70;
  margin: 0 0 12px;
}

.goodhero .art {
  font-size: 40px;
}

.flag {
  font-size: 10px;
  font-weight: 850;
  color: var(--red);
  background: #fff0ef;
  border: 1px solid #fecdca;
  padding: 4px 6px;
  border-radius: 5px;
  margin-bottom: 9px;
  display: inline-block;
}

.greenflag {
  color: var(--green);
  background: #ecfdf3;
  border-color: #abefc6;
}

.reason {
  margin-top: 10px;
  padding: 10px;
  background: #f8f7ff;
  border-radius: 8px;
  color: #55506d;
  font-size: 11px;
}

.detail-list {
  display: grid;
  gap: 12px;
}

.issue {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr;
  gap: 15px;
  padding: 16px;
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 14px;
}

.issue h3 {
  margin: 0 0 6px;
}

.issue p {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 14px;
}

.checklist {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  gap: 10px;
}

.check {
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 13px;
  display: flex;
  gap: 10px;
  align-items: start;
}

.check input {
  margin-top: 4px;
  accent-color: var(--purple);
}

.check span {
  font-size: 13px;
}

.footer {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  padding-top: 20px;
  margin-top: 45px;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 12px;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 14px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

@media (max-width: 800px) {
  .hero {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .hero-art {
    transform: none;
  }

  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .boards {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .audit-table {
    display: block;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .checklist {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .section-head {
    display: block;
  }

  .issue {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header>
  <div class="brand">
    UX<span>Lens</span>
    <span style="color:#a2a0b2;font-weight:500">/ case study</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tag">HEURISTIC AUDIT · REDESIGN</div>
</header>

<section class="hero">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Portfolio project · Concept demonstration</div>

    <h1>
      Find the friction.<br>
      <span style="color:var(--purple)">Design the fix.</span>
    </h1>

    <p>
      A transparent usability audit and redesign of a fictional demo
      storefront. Explore heuristic findings, severity priorities,
      and before-and-after interface concepts—without fabricated
      user-testing data.
    </p>

    <div class="actions">
      <button class="btn primary" onclick="showTab('comparison')">
        Explore redesign ↗
      </button>

      <button class="btn secondary" onclick="showTab('audit')">
        View heuristic audit
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="hero-art">
    <div class="art-top">
      <b>UX LENS / REVIEW BOARD</b>
      <span>DEMO ONLY</span>
    </div>

    <div class="art-title">
      A clearer path<br>from browse to buy.
    </div>

    <div class="mini-row">
      <div class="mini-card">
        <small>Review method</small>
        <b>10</b>
        <small>Nielsen heuristics</small>
      </div>

      <div class="mini-card">
        <small>Example findings</small>
        <b>3</b>
        <small>illustrative issues</small>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="progress"><span></span></div>

    <div style="font-size:11px;color:#c8c5ef;margin-top:8px">
      Concept redesign · no user metrics claimed
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="note">
  <b>Scope & honesty note:</b>
  This is a demonstration using a fictional storefront, not an audit
  of a real commercial app. The issues below are intentionally built
  into the “before” mockup as examples. Replace them with annotated
  screenshots and evidence from the real interface you choose to
  evaluate. No user tests or outcome statistics are claimed.
</div>

<nav aria-label="Project sections">
  <button class="tab active" data-tab="overview"
    onclick="showTab('overview')">Overview</button>

  <button class="tab" data-tab="audit"
    onclick="showTab('audit')">Heuristic audit</button>

  <button class="tab" data-tab="comparison"
    onclick="showTab('comparison')">Before / after</button>

  <button class="tab" data-tab="rationale"
    onclick="showTab('rationale')">Design rationale</button>

  <button class="tab" data-tab="checklist"
    onclick="showTab('checklist')">Evidence checklist</button>
</nav>

<!-- OVERVIEW -->
<section class="section active" id="overview">

  <div class="section-head">
    <div>
      <h2>Project overview</h2>
      <p>Evaluate an interface, identify friction, and make the reasoning visible.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card">
      <div class="small-label">01 / Evaluate</div>
      <h3>Use a consistent framework</h3>
      <p>
        Review the interface against Jakob Nielsen’s 10 usability
        heuristics. Record what is visible, where it occurs, and which
        heuristic it may affect.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <div class="small-label">02 / Prioritize</div>
      <h3>Fix what matters first</h3>
      <p>
        Assign critical, medium, or low priority based on potential
        impact and how much the issue blocks or slows a task. Explain
        the rationale for each rating.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <div class="small-label">03 / Redesign</div>
      <h3>Show the change clearly</h3>
      <p>
        Compare the original state with a revised concept. Link each
        design decision directly to a documented issue and its heuristic.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head">
    <div>
      <h2>Scope & deliverables</h2>
      <p>A focused case study with traceable evidence.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Heuristic audit table</h3>
      <p>
        Issue, interface location, heuristic, evidence, severity,
        and recommended fix.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>Annotated comparison boards</h3>
      <p>
        Before/after screens with numbered callouts and short explanations.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>High-fidelity redesign</h3>
      <p>
        Consistent typography, accessible contrast, clearer controls,
        and responsive layouts.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HEURISTIC AUDIT -->
<section class="section" id="audit">

  <div class="section-head">
    <div>
      <h2>Heuristic audit</h2>
      <p>Illustrative findings for the fictional demo storefront below.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    Severity here is a reasoned design-review priority, not a measured
    impact score. Confirm or revise it after examining the real product
    and its context.
  </div>

  <table class="audit-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Example issue & evidence</th>
        <th>Nielsen heuristic</th>
        <th>Priority</th>
        <th>Recommended improvement</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <b>A — Weak primary action</b><br>
          The “before” screen uses a low-contrast, small CTA that
          competes with surrounding content.
        </td>
        <td>
          #8 Aesthetic and minimalist design;
          #4 Consistency and standards
        </td>
        <td><span class="pill medium">MEDIUM</span></td>
        <td>
          Use one visually dominant, clearly labeled action with
          adequate size and spacing.
        </td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>
          <b>B — Search is difficult to discover</b><br>
          The “before” navigation has no visible search control,
          even though browsing a catalogue is a core task in this demo.
        </td>
        <td>#6 Recognition rather than recall</td>
        <td><span class="pill medium">MEDIUM</span></td>
        <td>
          Place a labeled search field in the expected header area
          and provide a clear focus state.
        </td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>
          <b>C — Product information is cramped</b><br>
          The “before” product cards use tiny text and crowded spacing,
          making key details harder to scan.
        </td>
        <td>
          #8 Aesthetic and minimalist design;
          #4 Consistency and standards
        </td>
        <td><span class="pill low">LOW</span></td>
        <td>
          Increase type size and spacing, align price/name hierarchy,
          and keep card patterns consistent.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="section-head">
    <div>
      <h2>All 10 heuristics — review checklist</h2>
      <p>Use this list when evaluating your chosen real interface.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>1. Visibility of system status</h3>
      <p>Does the interface communicate what is happening and what state it is in?</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>2. Match between system and real world</h3>
      <p>Does it use familiar language, concepts, and a natural order?</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>3. User control and freedom</h3>
      <p>Can people undo, cancel, or leave unwanted states easily?</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>4. Consistency and standards</h3>
      <p>Do similar controls and terms behave consistently?</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>5. Error prevention</h3>
      <p>Does the design prevent avoidable mistakes before they happen?</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>6. Recognition rather than recall</h3>
      <p>Are options and instructions visible when needed?</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>7. Flexibility and efficiency</h3>
      <p>Are common tasks efficient for new and experienced users?</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>8. Aesthetic and minimalist design</h3>
      <p>Does each element serve a purpose without unnecessary noise?</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>9. Help users recover from errors</h3>
      <p>Are errors explained clearly with a path to recovery?</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h3>10. Help and documentation</h3>
      <p>Is relevant help easy to find and act on?</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BEFORE / AFTER COMPARISON -->
<section class="section" id="comparison">

  <div class="section-head">
    <div>
      <h2>Before vs after</h2>
      <p>Side-by-side concept boards with three visible example issues.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    The storefront is fictional. These screens are illustrative interface
    concepts, not screenshots of a real website. Use annotated screenshots
    of your selected product for the final audit.
  </div>

  <div class="boards">

    <!-- BEFORE DESIGN -->
    <div class="board">
      <h3>Before · demo concept</h3>
      <p>Weak CTA hierarchy, hidden search, cramped product details.</p>

      <div class="browser">
        <div class="browserbar">● ● ● &nbsp; demo-store.local</div>

        <div class="shopnav">
          <span>dayform</span>
          <div class="links">
            <span>Shop</span>
            <span>About</span>
            <span>Bag</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="shopbody">

          <div class="shophero">
            <span class="flag">A · CTA hierarchy</span>
            <h4>Make room for everyday.</h4>
            <p>Thoughtful essentials for your daily routine.</p>
            <button class="old-cta">Explore</button>
          </div>

          <div class="small-label">Popular picks</div>

          <div class="product-grid">
            <div class="product">
              <span class="bad-marker">C</span>
              <div class="photo">🧴</div>
              <b>Daily cleanser</b>
              <small>$18.00</small>
            </div>

            <div class="product">
              <div class="photo">🫙</div>
              <b>Soft cream</b>
              <small>$24.00</small>
            </div>

            <div class="product">
              <div class="photo">🧼</div>
